Package: lmmresample
Title: Resampling Inference for Mixed Models of Densely Sampled Time Series
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ricardo", "Martínez-Flores", , "ricardo.antonio.martinezf@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8435-2710")),
    person("Hans", "Supèr", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Permutation and bootstrap inference for linear and generalized
    linear mixed-effects models fitted to densely sampled physiological time
    series such as pupillometry or EEG. Provides trial- and participant-level
    permutation under user-declared exchangeability, simulation-based
    calibration of the permutation null, family-wise error control with the
    max-t procedure, cluster bootstrap confidence intervals (percentile and
    bias-corrected and accelerated), and leave-one-subject-out diagnostics.
